       bytes at the end of the thread’s stack to act as the guard area for the
       stack (but see BUGS).

       If  _g_u_a_r_d_s_i_z_e  is 0, then new threads created with _a_t_t_r will not have a
       guard area.

       The default guard size is the same as the system page size.

       If  the  stack  address  attribute  has  been  set   in   _a_t_t_r   (using
       pptthhrreeaadd__aattttrr__sseettssttaacckk(3) or pptthhrreeaadd__aattttrr__sseettssttaacckkaaddddrr(3)), meaning that
